        {
          "title": "INDOOR LOCATIONING OF SMARTPHONES USING WIFI",
          "subtitle": "Oct 2012 - Dec 2012",
          "subComponenets": [
            {
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "The prolific advancement of the computing and networking technologies has made today’s networking devices smaller, more powerful and as ubiquitous and mobile as never before. And this has led to a greater need for connectivity and higher precision in locationing of devices. The need for outdoor locationing has been quite well served till now by technologies like Global Positioning System. But when it comes to indoor locationing, the “not so precise” GPS fails to deliver. In the recent years, Indoor Locationing has evolved as one of the most challenging area in network technologies.\nIn this research project, we have developed an end-user application that can determine, with approximate accuracy, the location of a user equipped with an android based smartphone within an area (preferably inside a building), which has one or more Wi-Fi network(s) with multiple Wi-Fi access points (beacon points) placed at different locations in the building."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
